# Copy to .env.local and adjust for your machine.
#
# API_URL is the backend the Next.js dev/build server proxies /api/* to.
# It is server-side only: the browser always calls same-origin /api.
# (There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL in the request path anymore - see below.)
#
# Canonical backend port: 8000. That matches docker-compose.yml, the Dockerfile
# healthcheck, and DEPLOYMENT.md, so leaving it unset keeps everything consistent.
#
# The dev engine is currently on :8010 only because the demo mock
# (~/gradepulse-demo) was squatting :8000. Either move the mock off :8000 and
# drop this file, or keep the engine on :8010 and set:
# API_URL=http://localhost:8010
#
# next.config.ts prints a warning at dev start if this resolves to a
# non-GradePulse engine, so you cannot silently end up on the mock.
# API_URL=http://localhost:8000
